{"name":"Perseverance","hex":"#acb3c7","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"perseverance","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Continuing in a course of action without regard to discouragement, opposition or previous failure."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/perseverance"}],"entries":[{"title":"Perseverance (rover)","blocks":[{"text":"Perseverance is a NASA rover that has been exploring Mars since February 18, 2021, as part of the Mars 2020 mission. Built and managed by the Jet Propulsion Laboratory, the car-sized rover was launched on July 30, 2020, from Cape Canaveral aboard an Atlas V rocket and landed in Jezero Crater, a site chosen for its ancient river delta that may preserve evidence of past microbial life."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a4/Perseverance-Selfie-at-Rochette-Horizontal-V2.gif/330px-Perseverance-Selfie-at-Rochette-Horizontal-V2.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Perseverance_(rover)","wikidata":"Q87749354"},{"title":"Persistence (psychology)","blocks":[{"text":"Persistence is a personality trait, describing an individual's propensity to remain motivated, resilient, and goal-driven in the face of challenges and difficulties they may encounter whilst carrying out tasks and working towards goals. Identified by psychiatrist C. Robert Cloninger in his Psychobiological Model of Personality, persistence more precisely refers to \"perseverance in spite of fatigue or frustration\". According to Cloninger, this perseverance demonstrates a psychological determination that is foundational in aiding an individual's long-term success in achieving goals."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Persistence_(psychology)","wikidata":"Q368671"},{"title":"Perseverance (ship)","blocks":[{"text":"Several ships have been named Perseverance."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Perseverance_(ship)","wikidata":"Q42896748"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b6/PIA23499-Mars2020Rover-FirstTestDrive-20191217a.jpg/500px-PIA23499-Mars2020Rover-FirstTestDrive-20191217a.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b6/PIA23499-Mars2020Rover-FirstTestDrive-20191217a.jpg/1280px-PIA23499-Mars2020Rover-FirstTestDrive-20191217a.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b6/PIA23499-Mars2020Rover-FirstTestDrive-20191217a.jpg/500px-PIA23499-Mars2020Rover-FirstTestDrive-20191217a.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":" Perseverance in the Jet Propulsion Laboratory near Pasadena, California","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APIA23499-Mars2020Rover-FirstTestDrive-20191217a.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/10/PIA19672-Mars2020Rover-ScienceInstruments-20150610.jpg/500px-PIA19672-Mars2020Rover-ScienceInstruments-20150610.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/10/PIA19672-Mars2020Rover-ScienceInstruments-20150610.jpg/1280px-PIA19672-Mars2020Rover-ScienceInstruments-20150610.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/10/PIA19672-Mars2020Rover-ScienceInstruments-20150610.jpg/500px-PIA19672-Mars2020Rover-ScienceInstruments-20150610.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APIA19672-Mars2020Rover-ScienceInstruments-20150610.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e3/Cameras_documenting_the_descent_and_landing_of_Perseverance_rover.png/500px-Cameras_documenting_the_descent_and_landing_of_